This project contains multiple components that are distributed under separate
licences. Unless otherwise specified in a file's header, the following rules
apply. Clauses 1 to 3 are subject to clause 4, which governs material this
project did not author and cannot license.

1. Source Code
   All source code files (including but not limited to C, Objective-C, GLSL,
   Python, shell, PowerShell, CMake and other build-system files) are
   licensed under the MIT License shown above. That is everything under
   include/, src/, shaders/, testbed/, tools/ and cmake/, and the build files
   at the top of the tree. The API reference generated from the public
   headers is the headers' own text, and is under this clause with them.

2. Documentation
   All files inside the docs/ directory and any other Markdown files that
   serve as documentation -- README.md, DESIGN.md, CHANGELOG.md, TODO.md and
   the notes beside the tools -- are licensed under the Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0).
   To view a copy of this license, visit:
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

3. Example Files
   All files inside the demos/ and examples/ directories are dedicated to the
   public domain via the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal (CC0) license.
   They are written to be copied into programs of your own, and no notice
   need go with them when they are.
   To view a copy of this dedication, visit:
   https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

4. Third-Party Material
   This project ships material it did not author: the Ubuntu Sans and Ubuntu
   Sans Mono fonts under fonts/ubuntu/, and the glyph atlas the build bakes
   from them into the library, renamed Fenestal Glyphs Sans and Mono (Ubuntu
   Font Licence 1.0, whose text and notice are beside the fonts and are built
   into every binary, because that licence requires them to travel with
   every copy); the Wayland protocol
   definitions under protocols/, and the code generated from them; the keysym
   table in src/backend/keysym_table.h, derived from X.Org's keysymdef.h;
   and everything else Part 1 of THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists.

   PART 1 OF THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md IS THE AUTHORITATIVE LIST, not the
   sentence above, which is a summary. Clauses 1 to 3 do not extend to any
   material recorded there, whether or not this clause names it. Part 2 of
   that file records what a build brings in from outside this repository --
   code compiled in from the build machine, and libraries placed beside the
   programs -- under its authors' licences likewise.

   The grants in clauses 1 to 3 extend to this project's own contribution:
   the code, the shaders, the generators, the harness and the prose around
   them. They do not extend to the third-party material, and nothing here
   grants a right in it that this project does not hold. Anyone
   redistributing this software, in source or binary form, must carry
   THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md with it.
